49
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:18,000
How has it been the transition from bedside nursing into like fix-me flight and then into

50
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
rotor?

51
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,040
I think that's a question that a lot of people have when they're considering whether they

52
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:27,760
want to get into this whole scene in general.

53
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:29,680
Yeah.

54
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:38,160
I think it was pretty similar to starting out in a sub-acute floor and going to an ICU,

55
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:48,400
like a busy ICU where you have these expectations and there's things that you're expected to

56
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:55,120
know and do in the ICU, kind of similar to me in that sense going from fixed-wing to

57
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,120
rotor.

58
00:04:56,120 --> 00:05:02,200
It was like, okay, now you've learned some things here, apply that and then add on top

59
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:11,360
of all of the other aeromedical stuff, aeronautical stuff, flight physiology and logistics that

60
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:18,200
you just don't see in an ICU or in a hospital or space.

61
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:22,560
The pre-hospital stuff is, it was quite overwhelming for me at first.

62
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,560
Yeah.

63
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:25,760
And also like the different patient populations.

64
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:32,080
In the nursing side, we tend to be pigeonholed into one specific patient set.

65
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:35,040
In our ICU, we never see kids.

66
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,360
We rarely see kids.

67
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,360
Right.

68
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:38,360
Yeah.

69
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:39,360
Definitely not babies.

70
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,360
Or pregnant women.

71
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:48,760
And I remember like a few times where you get a younger kid that comes into the ICU

72
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:57,200
or pregnant woman or post hemorrhage or whatever.

73
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,360
It's like, well, what do you mean?

74
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:02,360
Like, I don't know what I'm doing here.

75
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:05,920
Yeah, for sure.

76
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:16,040
So yeah, I think that aspect has been challenging for sure in a rotor setting.

77
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:20,320
