152
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:27,680
And then another question I had for you is like, you did all of your nursing time in

153
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:30,680
like the inpatient side.

154
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:36,760
Do you, how do you think about like in hindsight, do you think there's value in getting ER experience

155
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:37,760
as well?

156
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:43,640
So like most people come to flight either with ER experience or ICU experience.

157
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:46,560
Occasionally we see people have both, but normally like most nurses like follow one

158
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,560
track or the other.

159
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:49,560
What are your thoughts on that?

160
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:57,000
I think it would depend on where you're at.

161
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:05,240
I've talked to a few people recently that, you know, work full time in the ER and don't

162
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:13,480
really have a lot of experience with titrating trips or, or, you know, using multiple drips

163
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:19,800
to get a certain effect or a certain outcome.

164
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:28,080
I think it would be pretty helpful to have more experience with pediatrics.

165
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:33,480
Because that's always like a source of contention with, with people in general.

166
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:38,400
I think like the universal thought is, Peds are just challenging in general.

167
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:39,400
Yeah.

168
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:40,400
Kids are scary.

169
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:41,400
Yeah.

170
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,400
Sure.

171
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:47,720
I personally like had I thought about that ahead of time, like I probably would have

172
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:57,120
tried to do some more time in, in pediatrics, not so much in like NICU specific or, you

173
00:10:57,120 --> 00:11:01,960
know, working in the ER in the hopes that I would get some Peds here and there, but

174
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:06,400
like actually like go work in the PICU, go work in the Peds ED.

